WEBVTT

00:00:00.018 --> 00:00:01.797
Here is a simple example.

00:00:01.797 --> 00:00:06.132
Suppose three scores are ninety, ninety, and eighty.

00:00:06.132 --> 00:00:10.847
Row number gives the rows positions one, two, and three.

00:00:10.847 --> 00:00:14.117
It must choose a unique position for every row.

00:00:14.117 --> 00:00:17.552
Rank gives the two ninety scores rank one.

00:00:17.552 --> 00:00:23.209
The score of eighty then receives rank three, because two positions were used by the tie.

00:00:23.744 --> 00:00:30.641
Dense rank also gives the two ninety scores rank one, but the score of eighty receives rank two.

00:00:30.641 --> 00:00:36.910
This small example is worth remembering because it makes the difference among the three functions very clear.
